  "compare": [
    {
      "words": "see, observe, notice, note, remark, watch",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "see"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " 有“看”或“看到”的意思，是个通用词，使用范围最广。see 的使用范围虽然最广，但作“看”解时，不能用于祈使句。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "He looked round but "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "saw"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " nobody. 他转过头去看了一下，但没有看见什么。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "observe"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " 作“看到”或“注意到”解，强调的是“留心观察”。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "The search proved difficult, for the puma was often "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "observed"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " at one place in the morning and at another place twenty miles away in the evening. 搜寻工作被证实是很困难的，因为人们看到的这只美洲狮常常是早上在一个地方，而晚上又在20英里之外的另一个地方。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "notice"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " 作“注意到，发现”解，是表示在某种偶然的情况下，看到某种情况或事情。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c6",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "I happened to be walking in my garden when I "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "noticed"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " a huge number of snails taking a stroll on some of my prize plants. 我碰巧在花园里散步，突然看到许多蜗牛在我的一些心爱的植物上悠闲地爬着。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c7",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "note"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " 作“注意”解，是强调在做某事中，同时注意到某事。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c8",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "After consulting my railway timetable, I "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "noted"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " with satisfaction that there was an express train to Westhaven. 我翻阅了铁路时刻表，见有一班去韦斯赫温的快车，甚为满意。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c9",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "remark"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " 作“注意到，觉察”解，有时包含“评论”的意思。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c10",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "This outstanding originality of the newly-made film has been "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "remarked"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " by some critics. 这部新拍的影片有着鲜明的独到之处，受到了某些评论家的关注。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c11",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "watch"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " 表示“观看”或“监视”的意思，强调看到的人或物应处于运动状态。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c12",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "One day there were fewer people in the shop than usual when the woman came in, so it was easier for the detective to "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "watch"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " her. 一天，当那个女人进来时，该店里的人比平常少一些，所以侦探比较容易监视她。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
